WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.917 --> 00:00:04.216
- [Voiceover] This is an African Elephant.

00:00:04.216 --> 00:00:07.543
The largest land mammal in the world.

00:00:07.543 --> 00:00:10.627
So large that it dwarfed our backdrop.

00:00:10.627 --> 00:00:13.497
While conservation efforts
have made significant gains,

00:00:13.497 --> 00:00:16.123
the threat of poaching still looms over

00:00:16.123 --> 00:00:19.691
the future of this giant species.

00:00:19.691 --> 00:00:22.126
Distributed through
the deserts and jungles

00:00:22.126 --> 00:00:26.123
of Sub-Saharan Africa, their
large ears radiate heat

00:00:26.123 --> 00:00:28.790
to keep cool in the African sun.

00:00:30.006 --> 00:00:31.256
They eat a lot.

00:00:32.224 --> 00:00:37.020
Everything from roots,
fruits, grasses, and bark.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.770
And up to 600 pounds of it a day.

00:00:41.572 --> 00:00:44.900
The tusks are firm teeth
used for digging roots,

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.645
stripping bark from trees,

00:00:46.645 --> 00:00:50.838
and for fighting and defending themselves.

00:00:50.838 --> 00:00:52.943
Unfortunately, these ivory tusks can

00:00:52.943 --> 00:00:56.792
fetch quite a price on the black market.

00:00:56.792 --> 00:00:58.932
Poaching for the illegal ivory trade

00:00:58.932 --> 00:01:02.844
continues to be a devastating problem.

00:01:02.844 --> 00:01:05.261
This is the African Elephant.

00:01:09.565 --> 00:01:13.148
(soft instrumental music)

